    <!-- Hardware / LED help -->
    <string name="hw_section">Hardware: ESP32-C5 Status-LEDs</string>
    <string name="hw_intro">The Waveshare ESP32-C5-WIFI6-KIT has a 5-LED WS2812 RGB strip. At boot it flashes LED 0 red → green → blue → white (~150 ms each) as a self-test, then settles into the pattern below.</string>
    <string name="hw_led_power_title">LED 0 — status (idle colour + activity flashes)</string>
    <string name="hw_led_power_body">Idle colour: teal = sniffing and a BLE client connected, orange = sniffing only, blue = BLE only, dim white = neither. Briefly flashes green on every captured V2X frame, blue when sending over BLE, cyan when sending over USB, and pulses cyan/red when a BLE client connects/disconnects.</string>
    <string name="hw_led_user_title">LEDs 1–4 — sniffer / Ethernet / MQTT / activity</string>
    <string name="hw_led_user_body">• LED 1 (sniffer): red = stopped, green = running.\n• LED 2 (Ethernet, enc28j60/w5500 variants): off = no link, blinking = link up without an IP, solid green = 100 Mbit with IP, solid orange = 10 Mbit with IP.\n• LED 3 (MQTT): off = no Ethernet link, yellow = linked but not connected to a broker, green = connected.\n• LED 4: flashes blue when a V2X frame is captured while MQTT is connected, orange while it is not — each flash clears itself after ~50 ms.</string>
    <string name="hw_no_frames_title">No frames received although connected?</string>
    <string name="hw_no_frames_body">The sniffer starts on channel 1 (2.4 GHz). Real ITS-G5 / V2X traffic is at 5.9 GHz — RSSI −128 dBm and zero frames is normal until the channel is changed via the UART console (GPIO 11/12, not exposed on the breakout header without a probe).\n\nA test frame (payload DEADBEEF…) is sent on every boot and appears as the first entry in the frame log — this confirms USB and firmware are working.</string>
    <string name="hw_reset_title">Resetting the board from the app</string>
    <string name="hw_reset_body">The USB and BT connection screens have a "Reset on start" option that pulses RTS high for 100 ms and then low again. This soft-resets the ESP32-C5 without unplugging the cable and triggers a new test frame.</string>

